+// Near the viewer, the source's own ground layers add the detail its bake (the material's maps,
+// ~2.4 cm texels) cannot hold: the bake keeps everything it has (the layers' mix, photographed
+// plants painted on it) and takes the layers' variation finer than its texels, their colour over
+// their own colour at the bake's resolution. rgb: that colour ratio, a: its weight; normal: the
+// layers' fine slopes, in world coordinates, to add to the baked normal; roughness: theirs.
+const float DETAIL_NEAR = 15.0;
+const float DETAIL_FAR = 40.0;
+vec4 terrainDetail(vec3 geometricNormal, out vec3 slope, out float roughness) {
+  slope = vec3(0.0);
+  roughness = 1.0;
+  vec2 size = shadows.occlusionRect.zw - shadows.occlusionRect.xy;
